      "prompt": "subject_definitions\r\n<Subject 1> is the person defined by the character sheet in __MINIMAX_H3_REF_1__. Use that sheet as the sole character reference, preserving identity, hairstyle, wardrobe, and accessories without redesign.\r\n\r\nsummary\r\n[reference generation] A fifteen-second multi-shot dramatic cinematic scene. <Subject 1> stands inside a dimly lit apartment at night, breaking up with her partner over a phone call. The scene tracks her through three progressive shots, capturing her emotional transition from heavy hesitation to firm, tearful resolve.\r\n\r\nretention_analysis\r\n<Subject 1>: fully_preserved from __MINIMAX_H3_REF_1__ throughout [Shot 1], [Shot 2], and [Shot 3].\r\n__MINIMAX_H3_REF_1__ defines the character only, not the first frame, expression, pose, environment, or layout. Render one person; do not reproduce panels, repeated figures, labels, or reference backgrounds.\r\n\r\ndetailed_description\r\nPhotorealistic cinematic portraiture with moody low-key lighting, shallow depth of field, rain-streaked window bokeh, and natural skin textures. Use vertical 3:4 composition with cool blue exterior street lighting contrasting against warm interior shadows.\r\n\r\n[Shot 1] A medium shot lasting five seconds. <Subject 1> stands beside a large rain-streaked apartment window at night, holding a smartphone to her ear. City lights blur into soft golden and blue circles in the background. Her expression is heavy, eyes fixed downward with quiet sorrow. She speaks directly into the phone with a steady, subdued voice:\r\n<Subject 1>: \"It’s over, Mark. I can’t keep pretending we have a future.\"\r\n\r\n[Shot 2] At 00:05.000, the shot cuts to a closer bust-up framing. She listens intently to his agitated, muffled response coming through the phone speaker. A flicker of pain crosses her eyes and her jaw tightens. She takes a shallow, shaky breath, her eyes welling slightly with unshed tears, and replies:\r\n<Subject 1>: \"No, listening to you explain won’t change anything. It’s just... we’re done.\"\r\n\r\n[Shot 3] At 00:10.000, the shot cuts to an intimate facial close-up from the shoulders up. A single tear tracks down her cheek as she presses the end-call button on her phone screen. She lowers the phone, closes her eyes, and exhales a long, trembling breath of bittersweet release. The shot holds steady on her face as natural breathing concludes at the fifteen-second mark.\r\n\r\nKeep the character consistent throughout all cuts. No slow motion, broad comedy, readable text, subtitles, logos, flashbacks, or extra people visible on screen.\r\n\r\noverall_soundscape\r\nSoft ambient indoor room tone, gentle rain patter against glass, muffled, distorted voice murmurs from the phone speaker, clear spoken dialogue, and a soft electronic click as the call ends.\r\n\r\nnon_diegetic_music\r\nMinimalist, melancholic piano chords that swell softly during the second shot and fade into atmospheric silence.\n",
